# Preserve API tokens and .env keys

Never delete, revoke, rotate, or overwrite local API tokens, Strapi API tokens, or app `.env` keys unless the user **explicitly** asks.

## Allowed cleanup

- E2E / temporary users created for headless login or verification **may** be deleted after verify.
- Test artifacts (screenshots in `tmp/`, `.playwright-mcp/`) are not tokens — leave them unstaged as usual. Write verification screenshots to `tmp/` (gitignored).

## Never do as cleanup

- Do **not** delete or rotate Strapi API tokens (admin UI, DB `strapi_api_tokens`, or hashed access keys).
- Do **not** clear or rewrite app `.env` / `.env.development` / `.env.production` `VITE_API_KEY` (or similar) values.
- Do **not** wipe production or local token tables, even to “fix 401s” or tidy unused keys.

## If a token is missing

- Create a **new** token or reuse an existing unused one.
- Leave every existing token in place. Do not destroy, rotate, or truncate the table to make room.

```text
# ❌ BAD — cleanup / “reset tokens”
DELETE FROM strapi_api_tokens;
# or rotating VITE_API_KEY in apps/*/.env* without an explicit ask

# ✅ GOOD — missing key only
# create or reuse one token; write it into the app .env; leave all other tokens untouched
```
